00:02:35.633 --> 00:02:39.679
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:40.517 --> 00:02:42.795
Visal, would you like to volunteer abroad?

48
00:02:43.883 --> 00:02:48.405
Yes! Teaching children in Laos, I could share my English.

49
00:02:49.517 --> 00:02:51.063
What is one benefit?

50
00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:55.984
Working abroad, volunteers gain a global perspective.

51
00:02:57.083 --> 00:02:59.060
Which organization would you join?

52
00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:06.192
A water project. Building wells, I could contribute to a real community project.

53
00:03:07.333 --> 00:03:09.101
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:13.424
Grammar focus: Present participle clauses.

55
00:03:13.724 --> 00:03:14.911
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:15.617 --> 00:03:18.835
Working abroad, volunteers gain a global perspective.

57
00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:22.922
Living with a local family, she learned the language.

58
00:03:23.817 --> 00:03:26.687
Building a school, they made a lasting impact.

59
00:03:27.633 --> 00:03:30.829
The -ing clause and the main clause must have the same subject.

60
00:03:31.583 --> 00:03:36.639
Be careful! Don't say: Work abroad, volunteers gain a global perspective.

61
00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:42.480
Say: Working abroad, volunteers gain a global perspective.

62
00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:45.604
A participle clause starts with the -ing form.

63
00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:49.168
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:49.967 --> 00:03:51.548
Helping Across Borders.

65
00:03:51.848 --> 00:03:55.299
Volunteering abroad gives students a global perspective.

66
00:03:56.300 --> 00:04:00.401
Living with local families, volunteers enjoy real cultural exchange.

67
00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:05.350
Working with a local organization, they join a community project.

68
00:04:06.367 --> 00:04:09.492
Teaching and building, they contribute their time and skills.

69
00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:12.918
The experience can make a lasting impact.

70
00:04:14.033 --> 00:04:17.629
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:18.483 --> 00:04:21.841
blank abroad, volunteers gain a global perspective.

72
00:04:22.141 --> 00:04:25.110
A, Working. B, Work. C, Worked.

73
00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:30.225
The answer is A: Working.

74
00:04:31.383 --> 00:04:34.161
A group that works for a purpose is an blank.

75
00:04:34.461 --> 00:04:39.658
A, organization. B, experience. C, impact.

76
00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.304
The answer is A: organization.

77
00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:48.380
To give help or time is to blank.

78
00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:51.997
A, contribute. B, receive. C, borrow.

79
00:04:55.533 --> 00:04:57.742
The answer is A: contribute.

80
00:04:58.933 --> 00:05:02.294
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:06.020
What is one benefit of volunteering in another country?

82
00:05:14.817 --> 00:05:16.503
